# Q28 regression pin (REOPENED) — an enum `Float32` PAYLOAD stored from an
# f64 LOCAL must narrow to the payload width, not read 0.
#
# This is the exact shape canvas's event decode needs and the one that
# miscompiled to 0: `let fa = event_a(); Ev.Move(fa, fb)` where the payload is
# `Float32` but the value is a bare `Float` (f64) local. Before the Q28 fix the
# f64 value was stored width-blind (8 bytes) into the 4-byte f32 payload slot,
# and the `GetField` in the match read 0. Now the value is coerced to the
# payload's declared width before the store. RUNS + asserts stdout (204.75).
#
# NOTE: deliberately ONE enum construction. Two or more by-value enum
# constructions of a payload-carrying variant in a single function trip an
# UNRELATED drop-elaboration UAF crash on this branch (filed as Q31; it
# reproduces with purely-inline f32 payloads and zero coercion, so it is not the
# Q28 width defect). The struct pin 650 carries the full four-shape matrix
# (inline f32 / bare f64 / f32 local / f64 local) crash-free; this case isolates
# the enum-payload load-from-local path that canvas depends on.
enum Ev
  Move(Float32, Float32)
  Tick
end

def f64_a -> Float
  120.5
end

def f64_b -> Float
  84.25
end

def main
  let fa = f64_a()
  let fb = f64_b()
  match Ev.Move(fa, fb)
    Ev.Move(x, y) -> puts "#{x + y}"
    Ev.Tick       -> puts "tick"
  end
end
